# Sub-tick interpolation of a moby's painted extent and colour
# (scripts/check_feeder_subtick.sh --path moby-mask).
#   <bk2> | <V> | blob=<x>,<y> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>] [astep=<px>] [cstep=<n>]
#
# scripts/check_moby_subtick.sh answers for a moby's vertex and keyframe
# animation, by comparing host-side poses. It does not separate the two cells
# this row measures: the screen scale the moby is drawn at, which is its mask's
# pixel count, and the colour it is drawn in, which is that mask's mean.
#
# The two legs are a render-path selection with and without the moby path,
# terrain in both, so the mask holds the mobys alone and nothing of the world
# behind them.
#
# moby-crossfade: two mobys, named at the positions the tick at V drew them.
# (201.6,206.5) is the one that moves, 4.3 px across the interval while its
# mask grows 624 px to 788 px — the scale cell. (321.6,90.7) barely moves and
# barely resizes, and its mean colour steps 26 levels over the interval — the
# keyframe colour crossfade the movie is named for.
moby-crossfade.bk2 | 1801 | blob=201.6,206.5 blob=321.6,90.7 tol=1.0 step=4
